      "conditions": [
        "Vanquish, never convert: a converted Sister hands over no Hound, no component blueprint and no Tenet weapon",
        "Every vanquish drops exactly one random blueprint out of twelve, so four Sisters is the floor and about eight is the realistic average",
        "The Hound a vanquished Sister mails you arrives fully built but ungilded, and still needs rank 30, gilding, then rank 30 again to be worth anything",
        "A second Hound sharing a Model you already gilded is worth zero mastery, whatever its other parts",
        "A Parazon Mercy on the downed Candidate is what creates the Sister in the first place",
        "The Treasurer despawns if you take too long, and its Zenith crown is consumed on every Granum Void entry"
      ],
      "bonuses": [
        "Each vanquish also hands over her Tenet weapon and her own fully built Hound",
        "Component blueprints trade between players, so a missing Model can be bought outright; built parts and assembled Hounds never trade"
      ],
      "disclosures": [
        {
          "title": "the fast Sister loop",
          "body": "Solo, normal, not Steel Path, Capture on Hydra, Pluto. A squad raises the kill requirement inside the Granum Void, so run it alone. Waypoint a gold hand first, kill the capture target, then come back and insert the Zenith crown; if no hand has shown up halfway through the tile, restart, and if one spawns within roughly 200m of extraction the Sister may not appear at all. Inside the Void the spawn cap is about 20 enemies and nothing new arrives until that batch is dead, so stay on top of them with a chaining or nuking weapon rather than spreading out. Equip the Xoris: heavy-attack the Granum ghosts to charge it, then detonate on the captured Solaris target for a large time extension, and kill 25 Parvos units for the time triangles they drop. Kill the Treasurer every cycle for the next crown, and hit Replay on the white end screen to re-run instantly."
        },
        {
          "title": "which Core, Bracket and Stabilizer to keep",
          "body": "Only the Model earns mastery, so the other nine blueprints are stat and precept picks and duplicates cost nothing. Take Adlet for the 450 base shields and pair it with Cela (+15%) or Zubb (+10%): Reinforced Bond wants at least 343 base shields, and Urga at -5% is the only bracket that can miss, dropping a 350-shield Core to 332.5. Frak is the stabilizer pick for its Vazarin polarity and the cheapest material list of the three, all star-chart resources plus Nitain. The Hound a Sister mails you rolls its own Core, Bracket and Stabilizer, so check its base shields against 343 before you build Reinforced Bond around it."
        }
      ]
    },
